  "findings": [
    "The RAPIDS Conda environment and cuTile virtualenv are distinct, independently revisioned runtimes; they are not interchangeable.",
    "The current Docker RAPIDS executor intentionally omits PyTorch; torch absence is not a graph-executor defect and installing a second CUDA wheel stack is not indicated.",
    "The live Docker executor currently sees the RTX 3060 Ti and its health and graph capability GETs pass, but the service has no Docker health status in the running container.",
    "The current OpenAPI does not expose the historical /v1/knn/exact route. The available cuVS exact scan is an Arrow tile-artifact route, not proof of current semantic corpus admission.",
    "The historical semantic768 exact-oracle receipt remains bounded fixture evidence and itself records candidate population freeze blocked, live current cohort ineligible, and CAGRA comparison not run.",
    "CUDA 13.4 and TensorRT-RTX 1.6 were not installed or evaluated."
  ],
  "changesThisReview": [
    "docker/docker-compose.gpu.yml: add a future container healthcheck requiring HTTP health and CUDA availability; validated compose configuration only, not applied to the running container."
